{"n": 17, "kind": "paragraph", "text": "The daughter nucleus is too heavy compared to e+ and ν, so it carries\nnegligible energy (Ed ≈0). If the kinetic energy (Eν) carried by the\nneutrino is minimum (i.e., zero), the positron carries maximum\nenergy, and this is practically all energy Q; hence maximum Ee ≈ Q).", "book_id": "PHY12O", "chapter_num": 14, "page": "047"}
