{"n": 6, "kind": "list", "text": "Use the relativistic formula for energy:\nE 2 = c2p 2 + m 0 2 c4 = 9 × (6.63)2 × 10–22 + (0.511 × 1.6)2 × 10–26\n    ∼ 9 × (6.63)2 × 10–22,\nthe second term (rest mass energy) being negligible.\nTherefore, E = 1.989 × 10–10 J = 1.24 BeV. Thus, electron energies\nfrom the accelerator must have been of the order of a few BeV.", "book_id": "PHY12O", "chapter_num": 14, "page": "044"}
